# Lesson 2, new hand (Mike's texture pair, second hand): 13 HCP with poor texture, open reluctantly. Student sits South.
title: A reluctant opening
id: L02-32
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.1, 2.2
student: S
board: 38
dealer: E
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  974    AQT93  85     T63
  E  KT83   J76    AT93   Q8
  S  QJ65   K82    QJ74   KJ
  W  A2     54     K62    A97542

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1D*    = 13+ points, at least four diamonds
     key: 13 HCP plus 1 for the doubleton is 14, so you open, but reluctantly: no aces, and the queens and jacks are scattered. With two four-card suits, open the lower one.
     not 1S: With two four-card suits, which one did the lesson say to open?
     not Pass: Did you count the doubleton? 13 plus 1 is 14, enough to open, even if the hand looks poor.
     not 1NT: 1NT shows 15-17. Did you count 13 HCP?
     not *: With 14 points and two four-card suits, what does the lesson say to open?
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = 6-9 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = No game: at most 23
     key: Partner showed 6-9. 14 plus 9 is 23 at most, short of the 25 a game needs. Pass.
     not *: Did you add it up? 14 plus 6-9 can't reach 25.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your hand counts to 14, so it opens, but reluctantly: there are no aces,
  and the queens and jacks are spread around instead of backing up a long
  suit. Partner's 1NT showed 6-9 points and a balanced hand. Your side has
  at most 23, so you pass. North is declarer, because he bid no-trump
  first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E S3  S S5  W SA  N S4
  2   W S2  N S7  E SK  S S6
      note: West returns partner's suit.
  3   E S8  S SJ  W C4  N S9
  4   S HK  W H4  N H3  E H6
      note: Declarer's plan: run the hearts. The king first, the high card from the short side.
  5   S H8  W H5  N HA  E H7
      note: Back to declarer's hand.
  6   N HQ  E HJ  S H2  W C5
      note: Keep going.
  7   N HT  E C8  S D4  W C7
      note: Declarer's hearts are all winners now.
  8   N H9  E D3  S D7  W C9
      note: The last heart.
  9   N D5  E D9  S DQ  W DK
      note: Declarer leads a diamond to try to set up a trick in dummy.
  10  W CA  N C3  E CQ  S CJ
  11  W D6  N D8  E DA  S DJ
  12  E DT  S CK  W D2  N C6
  13  E ST  S SQ  W C2  N CT
      note: Dummy's ♠Q wins the last trick. 7 tricks: 1NT made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: run the hearts.

  1NT made, mostly thanks to partner's hearts. Hands like yours, with
  queens and jacks but no aces, often take fewer tricks than the point
  count suggests.
